{"availability":"available","full":"vayungodara/cliproxy-rs","name":"cliproxy-rs","description":"Rust rewrite of CLIProxyAPI: drop-in compatible proxy for Claude, Codex, Gemini and OpenAI-compatible providers","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":5,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-03T08:42:43Z","updated":"2026-10-04T03:13:11Z","license":null,"branch":"master","homepage":null,"topics":["ai-gateway","anthropic","claude","claude-code","cliproxyapi","codex","codex-cli","gemini","gemini-cli","llm","llm-gateway","llm-proxy","multi-account","openai","openai-api","opencode","proxy","rust","self-hosted"],"demo":null,"color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T05:04:48.221Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T05:04:48.221Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T05:04:48.221Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T05:04:48.221Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T05:04:48.221Z","stars":5,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["cliproxy-rs is a small server you run on your own computer. It lets your coding tools, such as Claude Code, Codex CLI or Cursor, use the AI subscriptions and API keys you already have, like a Claude Max plan or a ChatGPT plan, through one local address. A dashboard built into it shows which accounts work, how much of each plan's limits is left, and how to connect each tool.","It is a Rust rewrite of CLIProxyAPI. It reads the same config.yaml and the same account files, so you can switch between the two in either direction."],"features":["You pay for Claude and ChatGPT plans and want Claude Code, Codex CLI and your editor to share them, with the 5-hour and weekly limits of every account on one screen.","You have several Claude or Codex accounts and want requests spread across them, or moved to the next account when one reaches its limit.","A tool speaks only one API: the proxy translates between the Anthropic, OpenAI and Gemini formats, so an OpenAI-only tool can use a Claude account and the other way round.","You run CLIProxyAPI and want a smaller, faster-starting binary with the dashboard built in."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vayungodara/cliproxy-rs/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"c074991fda23cfccc09025900b6470af416f92e100cc6044d020599979b14cd1","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T05:04:48.221Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T05:04:48.221Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"cliproxy-rs is a small server you run on your own computer. It lets your coding tools, such as Claude Code, Codex CLI or Cursor, use the AI subscriptions and API keys you already have, like a Claude Max plan or a ChatGPT plan, through one local address. A dashboard built into it shows which accounts work, how much of each plan's limits is left, and how to connect each tool.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vayungodara/cliproxy-rs/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"In the dashboard, sign in with the CLIPROXYMANAGEMENTKEY line from keys.env and choose Connect account.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vayungodara/cliproxy-rs/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Run the same command again to upgrade; your config and keys stay as they are. docs/INSTALL.md shows how to start the proxy when you log in.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vayungodara/cliproxy-rs/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Keep access.api-keys set and server.host on 127.0.0.1 unless you need other machines to connect.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vayungodara/cliproxy-rs/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"c074991fda23cfccc09025900b6470af416f92e100cc6044d020599979b14cd1","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vayungodara/cliproxy-rs/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T05:04:48.221Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T03:13:11Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vayungodara/cliproxy-rs/blob/master/REA